    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d389">

                <pb facs="0496" n="482" xml:id="pg482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/7–2244: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-07-22T14:00:00+07:00">July 22, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received July 22—11:07 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1275. Rice at Sian telegraphs 18th and 20th [that] Chen Cheng being placed in
                    command reorganized 1st War Zone comprising Honan and Shensi provinces with HQ
                    [at] Sian. Chen has shown in press interviews conciliatory attitude toward
                    Communist question, asserting he will work to lessen Kmt–Communist tension, seek
                    political rather than military settlement, and will attempt relax present tight
                    blockade.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
